3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(2.5\\le Y\\le 6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423884} {:answer/id #uuid "a7f3918c-bbd9-5833-a7a6-c082875137c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(2\\le Y\\le 6.5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423887} {:answer/id #uuid "af7e026a-25c7-5309-a590-6ae712847280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(2.5\\le Y\\le 6.5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423889} {:answer/id #uuid "bc3fcaf7-6ccd-5abb-bed1-8fe2a55d99e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(2.5\\le Y\\le 7.5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af7e026a-25c7-5309-a590-6ae712847280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(2.5\\le Y\\le 6.5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423889} :answer-field/id #uuid "50791223-ab5f-58cd-9a39-6290ec407274" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a5c8fffc-11c1-576d-8ffb-d7561ffc582e" :question/math-academy-id "q-96643" :question/problem "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(2<X<7)$ can be approximated as" :question/worked-solution "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we first rewrite the strict inequalities as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X<7) & =P(3\\le X\\le 6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we extend the endpoints of the interval $3\\le X\\le 6$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3\\le X\\le 6) & ≈P(3-0.5\\le Y\\le 6+0.5) \\\\  & =P(2.5\\le Y\\le 6.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
